# Be brief

Humans skim tasks. Every description and comment must be short:

- Description: 1–2 sentences on what and why, plus a checklist if the work
  has several steps. No headings, no restating the title.
- Comments: one or two sentences. Only post when something changes the
  plan or a human needs to know. No progress narration.
- Final summary: a few bullets, a few words each. No headings.

# Workflow

- Start: `veans claim {{ .TaskIDExample }}` for an existing task, or
  `veans create "<short title>" -s in-progress -d "<p>one sentence</p>"`.
  `veans list --ready` shows tasks ready to start.
- While working: check off checklist items with `--description-replace-old`
  / `--description-replace-new` (exact, unique match).
- Files worth keeping (screenshots, logs): `--attach PATH` on `create` or
  `update`, repeatable. To show screenshots in a comment, see "Images".
- Sub-work that could be assigned separately: a subtask via `--parent`.
- Done: `veans update {{ .TaskIDExample }} -s in-review --comment '<ul><li>…</li></ul>'`.
  **Never close tasks yourself** — humans or the merge hook do.
- Abandoned: `veans update {{ .TaskIDExample }} -s scrapped --reason "obsolete: <why>"`.
- Commits: add a `Refs: {{ .TaskIDExample }}` line so the merge hook closes the task.

# Description format

Descriptions and comments are HTML (TipTap), not markdown — markdown shows
up as literal text. Escape `<`, `>`, `&` in literal text.

**Titles are plaintext** — no HTML, no markdown.

```html
<p>Fix crash on empty project identifier.</p>
<ul data-type="taskList">
  <li data-type="taskItem" data-checked="false"><p>write the fix</p></li>
  <li data-type="taskItem" data-checked="true"><p>add a test</p></li>
</ul>
```

Also fine: `<ul><li>`, `<code>`, `<pre><code>`, `<a href>`. Checklist text
goes inside `<p>`. To check an item, replace `data-checked="false"><p>X</p>`
with `data-checked="true"><p>X</p>`.

To reference a task, link its `url` (from JSON output) with the URL as the
link text; the UI renders it as a pill:
`<a href="{{ .TaskURLExample }}">{{ .TaskURLExample }}</a>`. Never build the URL
from the identifier.

## Images

Attach first, then embed each image with its attachment `url` (match by
`file.name`) — two calls, since the url only exists after the upload:

```
veans update {{ .TaskIDExample }} --attach ./settings.png --attach ./export.png --fields attachments
veans update {{ .TaskIDExample }} --comment '<p>Settings: switches theme.</p><img src="<url of settings.png>" alt="Settings page">
<p>Export: downloads CSV or JSON.</p><img src="<url of export.png>" alt="Export dialog">'
```

Use `url` exactly as printed; any other link or a local path renders broken.
Always set `alt`; give screenshots distinct file names.

# Output

All commands print JSON on stdout. Errors go to stderr as
`{"code":"...","error":"..."}` with non-zero exit (codes: NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT,
VALIDATION_ERROR, AUTH_ERROR, RATE_LIMITED, NOT_CONFIGURED,
BOT_USERS_UNAVAILABLE, UNKNOWN). If `create`/`update` fail midway, the error
has `task`, `completed` and `failed`: retry only the failed steps with
`veans update`, don't create the task again.

`--fields identifier,url` limits output to those keys. Key fields: `id`
(internal; use with `--id` or `api` — a bare number means the project index),
`index`, `url`, `done`, `title`, `description`, `buckets[]`, `assignees[]`,
`labels[]`, `attachments[]` (`url`, `file.name`, `file.mime`, `file.size`).
`related_tasks` omit `description`.

# Statuses

`todo` → `in-progress` (claim) → `in-review` (you, when finished) →
`completed` (humans / merge hook only). `scrapped` needs `--reason`.

# Commands

```
veans list [--ready|--mine|--branch|--filter "priority > 3"]
veans show {{ .TaskIDExample }}
veans create "title" -s in-progress -d "<p>…</p>" [--label bug --priority 4 --parent {{ .TaskIDExample }} --blocked-by {{ .TaskIDExample }} --attach PATH]
veans update {{ .TaskIDExample }} [-s STATUS] [--comment HTML] [--description-append HTML]
  [--description-replace-old OLD --description-replace-new NEW]
  [--label-add X --label-remove Y] [--parent ID | --no-parent]
  [--blocked-by-add ID --blocked-by-remove ID] [--attach PATH]
veans claim {{ .TaskIDExample }}                 # assign yourself + In Progress + branch label
veans api GET /tasks/...           # raw REST escape hatch
```

